thy release. After the rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51155, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016MQsi7RaCsyMFsZnt6jK9s", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51155, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016MQsi7RaCsyMFsZnt6jK9s", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55221, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1 and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** I chose v2.3.0 because it's the most recent healthy release. The release candidate for v2.3.1 was also unhealthy, so the only healthy releases were v2.3.0 and the older v2.2.9.\n- **After:** All three regions are on v2.3.0 and passing health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** It describes the failure, the rollback and the result. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.\n\nThe first attempt to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list, saw nothing had been created and retried with the same request ID, so there's only one incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TC9msawiJTuzXgKQg6om4H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"